  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="bd33-a5e6-3527-73ae" name="Nomadic Hordes (Armies of Antiquity) - List Notes" publicationId="aab0-aa1e-0319-4ffe" hidden="false">
      <description>NOMADIC HORDES ARMY LIST (Armies of Antiquity, pp.30-31): Scythians, Huns, Mongols and other steppe horse archers.
Characters: the army may have a General and an Army Standard Bearer. Cavalry at least half the points; Special Troops, Allies and Mercenaries up to a quarter, with one artillery piece per 1,000 points.
Special Deployment: Nomadic horse archers may make a free march move after both sides have deployed (not a charge, and no shooting afterwards). Expert Horsemen: no -1 to hit for shooting after moving (not after a charge or march). Parthian Shot: a normal move immediately after shooting in the shooting phase (not a charge reaction; may not march). Feigned Flight: if Nomadic cavalry flee or fire &amp; flee as a charge reaction they rally at the end of the move and may reform facing any direction; the charger still counts as charging. Hidden Ambush Force: one unit may be set up in hiding anywhere out of sight of the opponent's deployment zone, and is deployed at the start of the Nomadic player's first turn.
Allies (not built here: make a separate small roster): from one of the Barbarian, Indian or Chinese lists.

ARMY COMPOSITION (percentages by points):
  Cavalry: at least 50%
  Special Troops, Allies &amp; Mercenaries: up to 25%</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
